  "body": "This adds a separate one-use diagnostic for the remaining CPU boundary between existing PSSM shader submission, original render dispatch, and original RAM image retrieval. One bounded profiler records exact Python code/owner and C method/owner events, copies the existing submitted CPU matrices, and projects the retained legacy callback trace. It adds no render, task, RAM, GPU, GL, model, or ORT operation.\n\nThe separate sealed C\u2192ABBA protocol preserves the predecessor's 280 source pins and all exact-source CI, identity, host lease, terminal attestor, original archive replay, root/fresh acceptance, cleanup, and memory gates. All clocks/Texture remain ON; profiling follows C_ON, then OFF/ON/ON/OFF. The new allowance is five providers, 30 pairs, 8,064 named observer getters; it does not reuse a previous allowance. At most 168 events and 72 state snapshots per observed process; pipeline512KiB and aggregate encoded metadata832KiB.\n\nValidation: 33 new focused tests PASS; full suite1,285 PASS with seven skips in120.713s; synthetic mock smoke exit0. Retained wheel/source/AST audit matches installed image006 source; fresh whole-source review Critical0/Important0/Minor0. Source review covers implementationa78d9d87; final source09ad7e3 additionally records that review and rulings. Actual native execution is pending exact-source CI qualification.\n\nCPU locals are not GPU uniforms, render return is not GPU completion, and matching traces do not establish a shared GPU frame or observer neutrality. Original strict0/4FAIL and Stage7INCOMPLETE persist. No main merge or Cloud/registry publication.\n\nThe complete decision ledger follows, including every ruling and its cost if wrong.\n\n# Renderer pipeline boundary ledger\n\nPlan: superpowers/plans/2026-11-14-renderer-pipeline-sealed.md\nBasee708052f1dc94c70ab2f94bab2728a4935aeeaf5; feature/renderer-pipeline-sealed-v1.\n\nRuling: Continue inline on own branch with clean checkout \u2014 persistent user choice \u2014\nlater unrelated uncommitted changes remain unisolated.\nRuling: Observe existing CPU C-call boundaries instead of extracting GPU textures \u2014\nolder extraction demonstrably disturbed image updates; completed sampler/feedback/\nopaque-order cohorts already exist \u2014 this leaves GPU uniform/depth/HDR completion unproved.\nRuling: Use actual PSSM frame local feeding pinned setter call \u2014 public ShaderInput\narray getters are not assumed supported \u2014 source-reconstructed submission is not\ndirect GPU uniform interception and carries extra CPU timing overhead.\nPre-flight: profiler produces legacy callback projection plus new pipeline trace;\nnative binder supplies exact Python/C owners and private arrays; sealed validator\nrequires both, preserving complete raw replay/host/lifecycle controls. No old pin edits.\n\nTask1: Observer12 RED\u2192GREEN, structural binding5 RED\u2192GREEN, C_exception prefix\nRED\u2192GREEN; old/new focused45 PASS. Static AST found repo RAM target at85 rather\nthan assumed86; dedicated line assertion RED\u2192GREEN. Final new focused33 PASS5.470s.\nPinned retained PSSM/ShowBase wheel bytes match image006 installed manifest; repo\nRAM source parsed as data. No native imports/execution. Source audit retained.\nRuling: Keep static audit as a recorded byte/AST receipt rather than another\nproduction CLI \u2014 existing source closure pins the receipt and code \u2014 changing a\ndependency later requires a fresh explicit audit; static equality proves no C ABI.\nTask2: New explicit six-module sealed fork/case/scopes/workflow, synthetic15 RED\nfor missing protocol; then set/list closure error corrected at its source. Legacy\ncallback metadata is a projection from the single profiler, independently checked\nby the frozen predecessor validator. Full synthetic raw\u2192canvas\u2192I420 and whole\ncanary archive replay pass. Expanded costs C2592+A5472=8064,512KiB/832KiB retained.\nRuling: Retain previous callback_schedule/validation entry names in the fork \u2014\nthey express the same ON/OFF arm and preserve all existing consumers \u2014 naming\nalone does not imply a second observer; misunderstanding could overstate neutrality.\n\nFull suite1285 PASS7skip120.713s; mock s_curve smoke exit0 (synthetic only).\nFresh whole-source review a78d9d87: Critical0/Important0/Minor0; no fix pass needed.\nFinal: Ruling: Native C profiling ABI/owners/line/private-copy compatibility remains\nunproved \u2014 require the genuine new one-use canary \u2014 incompatible ABI spends the\ncanary allowance and stops this campaign without retry.\nFinal: Ruling: GPU uniforms/completion/shared-frame identity/cause remain unproved \u2014\nCPU submission/dispatch/RAM calls are the actual measured boundary \u2014 a GPU cause\ncannot be selected from equal sampled CPU traces.\nFinal: Ruling: Observer neutrality/timing are not assumed \u2014 state reads/profile hooks\nare intrusive and common clock/Texture stayON \u2014 any measured difference can include\nobserver or process timing effects.\nFinal: Ruling: No RSS or memory headroom claim \u2014 encoded832KiB/cgroup4GiB are distinct\nconstraints \u2014 unknown native allocation peaks remain a possible resource failure.\nFinal: Ruling: Source review grants no external CI/C/A acceptance \u2014 authenticate exact\nCI, originals, terminal attestor/liveheldhost/root+fresh gates separately \u2014 a failed\ngate stops downstream providers and leaves partial evidence, not a successful cohort.\nFinal: Ruling: Officialmodel/ORT0 and originalstrict0/4FAIL/Stage7INCOMPLETE persist \u2014\nthis observes the camera path only \u2014 driving/model/ranking conclusions remain absent.\nFinal: Ruling: Do not re-review unchanged280 predecessor files \u2014 root independently\nbyte-verified all280 and relevant fork gates were reviewed \u2014 inherited undiscovered\ndefects remain possible and are not covered by a fresh complete predecessor audit.\nFinal: Ruling: Keep own Drafts unmerged and Cloud/registry unpublished \u2014 continued\nexecution authorizes bounded diagnostics/owned branches, not publication \u2014 no main\ndeployment or finished original strict result is delivered by this campaign.\nDeferred minors: none. All declined-to-judge items above are explicitly ruled on.\nPre-native main48e79a7e and seven old workflow counts verified unchanged.\n",
